    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPrivate Waterfront Estate in the West of Ireland\n\nOccupying a spectacular waterfront position on the shores of Lough Meelagh, Knockranny Estate extends across a distinguished about 45 acre peninsula with 0.8 km of private shoreline. Surrounded by mature woodland, pastures and unspoilt countryside, the estate enjoys a remarkable sense of privacy and seclusion within one of the most picturesque settings in the west of Ireland. \n\nAt the heart of the estate stands Knockranny House, a historic country residence dating from circa 1820. Occupying an elevated position overlooking the lake and surrounding grounds, the residence offers an extraordinary canvas for restoration and the opportunity to revive a distinguished private estate within an exceptional waterfront setting. \nDirectly across the lake lies the esteemed Kilronan Castle Estate. Both properties formed part of the wider King-Tenison estate, whose influence shaped this landscape for generations. This shared heritage lends Knockranny a rare provenance and places it among the area's most historically significant private estates. \n\nComplementing the principal residence is a collection of original stone stables, coach houses and estate buildings arranged around a traditional courtyard. Rich in character and integral to the estate's heritage, these structures provide considerable scope for restoration and ancillary uses, subject to the necessary consents. \n\nThe estate's natural setting is among its most compelling attributes. Protected by mature trees and natural screening, the property enjoys complete privacy while retaining direct access to the shoreline. The combination of extensive waterfront, historic architecture and exceptional seclusion creates an opportunity seldom encountered in today's market. \n\nKnockranny Estate represents a unique offering: a historic waterfront estate of scale, provenance and character, presenting the opportunity to revive a private estate of exceptional character and significance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Distinguished lakeside peninsula on about 45 acres of mature woodland and pasture</li><li>0.8 km of private shoreline along Lough Meelagh</li><li>Historic c.1820 country residence offering an idlyllic canvas for restoration</li><li>Original stone stables, coach houses and courtyard buildings offering exceptional scope for ancillary uses (SPP)</li><li>Complete privacy within a secluded and unspoilt natural setting</li><li>Once-in-a-generation opportunity to restore a historic Irish estate</ul>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Cianan Duff"
      }
